CDAP Wrangler Enhancements
Byte Size and Time Duration Parsers
New Features
1. Unit Parsing Support
Wrangler now natively supports parsing of:

Byte Size Units:

Unit	Description	Base Value
B	Bytes	1
KB	Kilobytes	1000 bytes
MB	Megabytes	1000² bytes
GB	Gigabytes	1000³ bytes
TB	Terabytes	1000⁴ bytes
PB	Petabytes	1000⁵ bytes
KiB	Kibibytes	1024 bytes
MiB	Mebibytes	1024² bytes
GiB	Gibibytes	1024³ bytes
TiB	Tebibytes	1024⁴ bytes
PiB	Pebibytes	1024⁵ bytes
Time Duration Units:

Unit	Description	Base Value
ns	Nanoseconds	1
us	Microseconds	1000 ns
ms	Milliseconds	1000² ns
s	Seconds	1000³ ns
m	Minutes	60×1000³ ns
h	Hours	60²×1000³ ns
d	Days	24×60²×1000³ ns

2. New aggregate-stats Directive
Aggregates columns containing byte size and time duration values.

Syntax:

javascript
aggregate-stats :<size_column> :<time_column> <output_size_col> <output_time_col> [size_unit] [time_unit] [aggregation_type]
Parameters:

Parameter	Required	Description	Default
size_column	Yes	Source column with byte sizes	-
time_column	Yes	Source column with time durations	-
output_size_col	Yes	Target column for size results	-
output_time_col	Yes	Target column for time results	-
size_unit	No	Output unit for sizes (e.g., "MB")	Bytes
time_unit	No	Output unit for time (e.g., "s")	Nanoseconds
aggregation_type	No	"total" or "average"	"total"
Examples:

Basic aggregation:

javascript
aggregate-stats :data_size :response_time total_size total_time
With unit conversion:

javascript
aggregate-stats :file_size :processing_time size_mb time_sec MB s
Average calculation:

javascript
aggregate-stats :bytes_sent :latency avg_size avg_time MB ms average
Implementation Details
Grammar Changes
Added to Directives.g4:

antlr
// Lexer rules
BYTE_SIZE : Number BYTE_UNIT;
TIME_DURATION : Number TIME_UNIT;

// Fragments  
fragment BYTE_UNIT : [bB] | [kK][bB] | [mM][bB] | [gG][bB] | [tT][bB] | [pP][bB] 
                   | [kK][iI][bB] | [mM][iI][bB] | [gG][iI][bB] | [tT][iI][bB] | [pP][iI][bB];
                   
fragment TIME_UNIT : [nN][sS] | [uU][sS] | [mM][sS] | [sS] | [mM] | [hH] | [dD];

// Parser rules
value : String | Number | Column | Bool | byteSize | timeDuration;
byteSize : BYTE_SIZE;
timeDuration : TIME_DURATION;
New Classes
Class	Location	Purpose
ByteSize	wrangler-api/src/main/java/io/cdap/wrangler/api/parser/	Parses "10MB", "1.5GiB" etc.
TimeDuration	wrangler-api/src/main/java/io/cdap/wrangler/api/parser/	Parses "500ms", "2h" etc.
AggregateStatsDirective	wrangler-core/src/main/java/io/cdap/wrangler/api/directive/	Implements aggregation logic
Usage Examples

1. Parsing in Recipes
javascript
parse-as-size :file_size_bytes "MB"  // Converts to megabyte values
parse-as-time :response_time "s"     // Converts to seconds

2. Aggregation Pipeline
javascript

aggregate-stats :bytes_transferred :processing_time total_bytes total_seconds MB s;
set-column :avg_rate "total_bytes / total_seconds";
